  "method": "Visual inspection of final source-matched generated stills, same-camera AFM comparison, and actual browser captures; supported by native mesh/contact checks and independent instrument reviews. Review sheets preserve full frames and aspect ratios without retouching.",
  "reviewed_views": {
    "stills": "All seven overviews and working areas; Nikon focus controls, Zeiss stage/support, probe slots/recesses, transfer adjuster/heater supports, bonder heater, and four AFM construction views.",
    "browser": "All seven instruments in Interactive and Photo modes, four AFM operation states, and three transfer mechanism/clearance views.",
    "comparison": "Preserved old AFM handle and final stowed/deployed handle, with matching camera and framing.",
    "robotics": "Final generated gripper turn still; robot motion/media provenance verified separately in the robot package."
  },
  "observations": [
    "The AFM blade folds downward into a real rounded door pocket. The deployed blade rotates outward/upward from the top hinge, leaving the pocket visible; closed and restowed browser captures show the recessed handle.",
    "AFM open-door and keeper views show pocket walls/back pan, hinge shaft, seal seating, cylindrical keeper and bored receiver. The visible construction is improved; the concealed latch catch is unresolved and represented by the existing state interlock.",
    "The delivered Nikon left focus controls, Zeiss longitudinal stage opening and open support fork, and probe guide slots and recessed control wells match the corrected construction stills. Independent review found no obvious missing assemblies or stale geometry in the Interactive/Photo captures.",
    "Transfer live closeups retain a fully round sample-X handwheel above the table, compact vertical adjuster with engaged shaft, separate cylindrical supports/clamps, and visible cable routing. Heater supports and preload rods remain distinct in the detail render.",
    "The bonder has an opaque metal spool, distinct satin frame and polished shafts, silver prismatic wedge, and a thin textured insulating heater jacket with separate folded liner and air gap.",
    "Tweezers were reviewed and retained; the tray and pickup seat remain benchmark fixtures rather than claims about the photographed instrument.",
    "The live table and metal parts retain the existing reflection/lighting implementation; all public JavaScript rendering modules match the baseline. Photo captures display the same corrected geometry but retain visible low-sample noise."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Dimensions, hidden construction and physical parameters are estimates and are not manufacturer-calibrated.",
    "Visual inspection and sampled motion/contact checks do not certify every possible part pair, instrument configuration or arbitrary robot motion.",
    "Photo inspection used at least eight samples per model. These inspection screenshots are not converged beauty renders; the viewer refines the image while stationary.",
    "Some small features are partly obscured by browser camera angles, including the Nikon outer left dial face and probe upper guide opening; the construction stills show them more clearly.",
    "Cables retain prescribed visual deformation without cable contact, mass, tension or elastic dynamics. The contact benchmark uses a parallel gripper without an articulated robot arm.",
    "Two intended fixed AFM mounting seams retain 1.2219 micrometers of Boolean/bevel overlap within the recorded 2 micrometer allowance. Moving-part checks use strict tolerances without that exemption."
  ],
